.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_BODY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_body \- access the buffered request body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const void *chttpsvr_req_body(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                               size_t *len_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a pointer to the buffered bytes of the request body.  When
len_out is not NULL, the length of the body in bytes goes into it.

The result is NULL, with 0 stored in len_out, when the request has no
body.  It is the same for a request of a streaming route that was
registered with chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler, because the
server never reads the body of such a route ahead of the handler.
Use chttpsvr_req_read there instead.

The buffer is valid until the handler call returns.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
